    "Bridge": "connection topology classification; does not itself authorize bridging",
    "Path": "traversal topology classification; does not itself authorize traversal",
    "Lane": "bounded path-channel topology classification; generic topology realized through admitted lane systems",
    "Route": "ordered path-selection topology classification; does not itself authorize routing",
    "Pattern": "recurring or structured arrangement topology classification; does not itself authorize replication, execution, or control",
    "Busline": "shared linear passage topology; may later be realized logically or physically but does not itself assert hardware, signaling, connectivity, access, execution, or authority",
    "Transmission": "passage topology describing a transmission-oriented passage structure; does not itself perform or authorize transmission",
    "Connection": "passage topology describing a connection-oriented passage structure; does not itself establish or authorize connectivity",
    "Track": "defined passage course/topology classification; does not itself authorize traversal, routing, execution, persistence, or control",
    "Rail": "guided passage topology classification; does not itself assert physical railway infrastructure or authorize traversal, routing, execution, persistence, or control"
